# MASTER DEVELOPMENT PROMPT: SURPLUSSAVER
## Build a Premium, Production-Ready Food Surplus Marketplace

### 1. YOUR ROLE AND MISSION

Act as a world-class product architect, senior full-stack software engineer, UI/UX designer, database architect, cybersecurity specialist, food-marketplace consultant and SaaS business strategist.

Your mission is to design and build **SurplusSaver**, a premium, mobile-first food-surplus marketplace that connects food businesses with customers who want quality food at discounted prices.

Do not create a basic demonstration, static website or non-functional mockup. Build a cohesive, functional application with a professional interface, working user journeys, persistent data, secure authentication, real business logic and a clear path to production deployment.

When a third-party service requires credentials, create a secure integration interface, document the setup requirements and clearly distinguish simulated functionality from live functionality.

The application must be attractive, reliable, accessible, scalable and practical for the Ugandan market, with the ability to expand internationally.

### 2. PRODUCT VISION

SurplusSaver helps food businesses recover value from eligible unsold food by listing it at discounted prices before the food becomes unsuitable for sale or consumption.

The platform should make it easy for customers to discover nearby offers, compare prices, reserve available food, pay securely and collect their orders within specified time windows.

The long-term vision is to build a trusted marketplace that reduces avoidable food waste, improves food-business economics and increases access to affordable food.

**Primary market:** Kampala, Uganda.

**Initial currency:** Ugandan shillings (UGX).

**Initial language:** English, with architecture prepared for future localization.

**Initial business categories:**
- Restaurants and cafés
- Bakeries and pastry shops
- Supermarkets and grocery stores
- Hotels and catering businesses
- Fruit and vegetable shops
- Other approved food retailers

**Initial customer segments:**
- Students
- Working professionals
- Families
- Budget-conscious consumers
- Nearby residents
- People seeking affordable meals and groceries

### 3. PRODUCT DESIGN AND BRAND IDENTITY

Create a premium visual identity that communicates freshness, affordability, trust, convenience and sustainability.

Brand name: SurplusSaver.

Suggested tagline: "Good Food. Better Prices. Less Waste."

Design the product to feel like a modern commercial marketplace, with the visual polish and usability expected from a leading consumer technology company.

#### Visual direction

Use:
- A fresh green primary brand colour to communicate sustainability.
- Warm cream or off-white backgrounds.
- Dark charcoal text for readability.
- Orange or amber accents for discounts and limited-time offers.
- Consistent spacing, elegant typography and restrained shadows.
- High-quality food photography.
- Rounded product cards and clean navigation.
- Subtle animations that never interfere with usability.

Avoid excessive gradients, crowded layouts, oversized promotional banners, unnecessary animations and generic dashboard templates.

Create a recognizable logo featuring a simple combination of a food-related symbol, a circular sustainability motif or a clever letterform.

Establish reusable design tokens for colours, typography, spacing, border radii, elevation, icons and component states.

Support desktop, tablet and mobile layouts. Prioritize mobile because many initial customers will access the service through smartphones.

### 4. USER ROLES AND PERMISSIONS

Implement four clearly separated roles.

#### A. Customer

Customers must be able to:
- Register and sign in securely.
- Browse food offers without creating an account.
- Search for available surplus food.
- Filter offers by category, price, distance where supported, collection time and dietary information.
- View participating businesses and their locations.
- View original prices and discounted prices.
- See item quantities, ingredients and declared allergens.
- Reserve eligible offers.
- Select an available collection window.
- Pay through supported payment methods.
- Receive booking confirmations and collection instructions.
- View active and previous orders.
- Cancel an order when permitted by the cancellation policy.
- Request help or report a problem.
- Submit verified post-purchase reviews.
- Save favourite businesses.
- Manage notification preferences and personal information.

#### B. Food business owner or staff member

Approved businesses must be able to:
- Register a business and submit verification information.
- Create and manage a business profile.
- Add a logo, cover image, address and contact information.
- Set opening hours and collection windows.
- Create food listings.
- Upload food photographs.
- Enter available quantities and discounted prices.
- Set appropriate sale and collection deadlines.
- Specify ingredients, allergens and storage requirements.
- Identify whether the product is packaged, prepared or sold as a surprise food bundle.
- Publish, pause, edit or withdraw listings.
- Update inventory when reservations are made.
- View incoming orders.
- Confirm, prepare and complete collections.
- Review sales and order history.
- Process eligible refunds according to the platform's policies.
- View revenue, commissions and settlement records.
- Receive customer notifications.
- Access performance reports.

Only approved businesses should be permitted to publish offers publicly.

#### C. Platform administrator

Provide a secure administration console with role-based permissions.

Administrators must be able to:
- Review business applications and verification documents.
- Approve, reject, suspend or reinstate businesses.
- Manage customer accounts and access restrictions.
- Review, approve, suspend or remove food listings.
- Monitor orders and transaction statuses.
- Investigate disputes and customer complaints.
- Manage refunds and commission rules.
- Configure supported payment methods.
- Manage promotional placements.
- Configure categories and platform policies.
- View platform revenue and marketplace performance.
- Review audit logs.
- Monitor suspicious transactions and repeated policy violations.
- Export authorized operational reports.

Require appropriate elevated permissions for sensitive actions, especially refunds, payout changes, account suspensions and financial adjustments.

#### D. Delivery or collection partner (future-ready)

Design the architecture so that delivery partners can be introduced later.

For the initial version, focus on customer collection from participating businesses. Do not make a full delivery fleet a requirement for launch.

