Implement:
- Secure registration and sign-in.
- Email verification where appropriate.
- Secure password recovery.
- Role-based access control.
- Server-side authorization for every sensitive operation.
- Input validation and output encoding.
- Protection against common web vulnerabilities.
- Rate limiting on sensitive endpoints.
- Secure session and cookie configuration.
- CSRF protection where applicable.
- Appropriate content security policies.
- Secure upload validation.
- Payment webhook verification.
- Audit logging for administrative and financial operations.
- Data retention and deletion procedures.
- Secure secret management.

Use least-privilege access for database operations and external integrations.

Ensure customers cannot view other customers' private orders, business owners cannot access competitors' private financial records, and unauthorized users cannot access administrative functionality.

Design privacy notices and consent flows suitable for applicable Ugandan data-protection requirements, including the Personal Data Protection Office framework where relevant.

Collect only necessary personal data. Avoid exposing exact customer locations to other users without a legitimate, disclosed reason.

Never put secrets, API keys or service-role credentials into frontend source code.

